// ============================================================================
// subspace_null.kn — TurboKain 24: Baseband Spatial Subspace Projection (RBSPE)
// Real-Time Directional RFI Excision & Coherent Celestial Phase Preservation
//
// Theoretical Foundation:
//   Standard RFI blanking tools (sk_gate) wipe out entire time-frequency blocks
//   when transmitters flare, permanently discarding astronomical science data.
//
//   subspace_null ingests dual-polarization baseband voltage streams (pol0, pol1),
//   estimates the 2x2 spatial covariance matrix R_xx = 1/N sum x * x^H, and computes
//   its closed-form Hermitian eigen-decomposition:
//     1. Condition Ratio gamma = lam1 / lam2: Unitless eigenvalue contrast.
//        Thermal noise yields gamma ~ 1.0 - 2.5; directional RFI yields gamma >= 5.0.
//     2. Dominant Interference Eigenvector u_rfi: Maps the spatial steering vector
//        of the terrestrial transmitter.
//     3. Orthogonal Subspace Projector P_perp = I - u_rfi * u_rfi^H: Projects deep
//        spatial nulls (>30 dB) directly toward the RFI source.
//     4. Phase-Preserving Voltage Streaming: x_clean = P_perp * x.
//        When no RFI is detected (gamma < gate), P_perp defaults to identity I_2,
//        passing thermal noise with zero distortion.
//
// Semantics & Decision Ladder:
//   * L3 converge: cov2x2_eigen verified against closed-form spec with random(8) fuzz.
//   * L2 law: covariance_psd, projection_idempotent, rfi_condition_ratio.
//   * L1 world/patch: SubspaceAuthority ↔ SubspaceMirror tracking spatial null audit.
//   * Memory: Dual-channel streaming buffers, +32 byte SIMD padding, single decay.
//
// Exit codes: 0 searched, 1 help / prove FAIL, 2 error.
// ============================================================================

